    // ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // F-C4-576 (W8, 4APP4 Coder-4) — java.util.AbstractMap$SimpleEntry /
    // $SimpleImmutableEntry FULL ENTRY LAW.
    //
    // OpenJDK (java/util/AbstractMap.java: JDK 8..21, unchanged):
    //   SimpleImmutableEntry(K key, V value) — stores the pair;
    //   getKey() → key;  getValue() → value;
    //   setValue(V) → UnsupportedOperationException (immutable variant);
    //   toString() → key + "=" + value;
    //   equals(o)  → o instanceof Map.Entry && eq(key, getKey) && eq(value, getValue);
    //   hashCode() → (key==null ? 0 : key.hashCode()) ^ (value==null ? 0 : value.hashCode())
    // ($SimpleEntry: same ctor/getKey/getValue/equals/hashCode; setValue swaps and returns the OLD value.)
    //
    // ROOT (live, W8, TWO titles, one bridge gap):
    //   (a) Nextcloud 35.0.2 — the Dagger injector map iteration:
    //       ImmutableMap$Builder.put ×272 (REAL Class keys, probe o334...)
    //       → RegularImmutableMap.create(136, entries) ✓ → merge walks
    //       EntrySet.asList → EntrySet$1.get → materializes
    //       AbstractMap$SimpleImmutableEntry(o482, key=o334/Class, value=o64/Provider)
    //       — the ctor ran with REAL args — but the bridge had NO law for
    //       this JDK class, so getKey() answered the typed-default NULL →
    //       merge pc=49 "Class.getName on null" NPE → the whole
    //       DispatchingAndroidInjector build dies → androidInjector() null
    //       → checkNotNull IAE ×8 at every AndroidInjection.inject site
    //       (4 activities + 4 providers) → NC-M1 frozen.
    //   (b) Thunderbird v24 — j$.time.ZoneId.<clinit> builds its zone map
    //       from Map.Entry[]/SimpleImmutableEntry pairs; the same null
    //       getKey unwound the desugared java.time bootstrap.
    // The law materializes the pair as heap fields "key"/"value" on the
    // receiver and serves the whole protocol from them. Fans out to every
    // Guava/Dagger/java.time/collection consumer in the corpus.
    // ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
